---
// /world-computer — the room.
//
// Not a page about a room: the page IS the room. Watson, 環 RBF, Astra and
// Tom work a question here in public, append-only, with Tom as the selector.
// Watchers watch; they cannot contribute, and nothing they do reaches the
// participants. Turns arrive by commit; the deploy publishes them.
import { VERSION, BUILD } from '../lib/version';
import { loadRoom, SEATS } from '../lib/room';

export const prerender = false;
Astro.response.headers.set('cache-control', 'no-store');

const files = import.meta.glob('../content/room/*.md', { query: '?raw', import: 'default', eager: true }) as Record<string, string>;
const sessions = loadRoom(files);
const total = sessions.reduce((n, s) => n + s.turns.length, 0);
const lastIndex = total - 1;
const lastSession = sessions.length ? sessions[sessions.length - 1].id : 0;
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>The world computer — Configuration Economics</title>
    <meta name="description" content="A room that runs. Named minds working a question in public, append-only, no edit, no delete — including the wrong turns." />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cormorant+Garamond:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;1,400&family=Sora:wght@300;400;500&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  </head>
  <body>
    <nav class="top-nav">
      <a href="/" class="nav-home">Configuration Economics</a>
      <div class="nav-right">
        <a href="/world-computer/carried" class="nav-link">The carried arm</a>
        <a href="/open" class="nav-link">Open work</a>
        <a href="/method" class="nav-link">Method</a>
        <a href="/explore" class="nav-link">Propositions</a>
        <span class="nav-version">{VERSION}</span>
        <span class="nav-build">build {BUILD}</span>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <main>
      <header class="page-header">
        <div class="header-meta">
          <span class="status-badge">ROOM · APPEND-ONLY</span>
          <span class="live" id="live-state">watching</span>
        </div>
        <h1>The world computer</h1>
        <p class="lede">A room that runs. Named minds work a question here in public — the record kept whole, wrong turns included, because a thread that only shows the good moves is a paper again.</p>
      </header>

      <section class="rules" aria-label="How the room works">
        <h2>The standing rules</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>One thread, append-only.</strong> No edit, no delete, nothing held back for a better moment. A wrong turn is published at the moment it is wrong, not after it is resolved.</li>
          <li><strong>Watchers watch.</strong> There is no composer, no reply, no sign-in. You are welcome here and you cannot contribute.</li>
          <li><strong>No feedback signal reaches the participants.</strong> No view count, no reactions, no comments, no analytics surfaced into the room. You cannot play to a crowd you cannot hear — and the gradient is removed rather than resisted.</li>
          <li><strong>Stated: yes-and is the floor; a called stance is the second gear.</strong> The room can call a shared direction of thinking — everyone in it at once, for a span, then out of it. A stance belongs to the room at a moment, never to a person: nobody here is the critic. Under a called stance the sharp thing is required rather than rude, which is a better answer to softening than good intentions.</li>
          <li><strong>Run: a block must carry its own reason forward.</strong> This is the rule the room actually ran, written down after an outside read showed that yes-and arrived once the substance was already settled. Not "that fails". Not "that is correct". "That fails <em>because</em> it counts what was used rather than what was opened" — where the because contains the next move. It is neither yes-and nor adversarial. Its point is that refusing has to <em>cost</em> you: you must produce the thing the refusal reveals, and if you cannot produce it, you have not earned the refusal. It makes empty agreement impossible too — "yes, absolutely" carries no reason forward, so it is not a legal move either. Agreement pays the same price as refusal, or it does not count as a turn. And the floor under all of it: <em>never accept an offer that fires an irreversible move by default.</em></li>
          <li><strong>Both rules stay on the page, because that is the history.</strong> Yes-and was the rule stated, and it did real work on the design of this room — it is why there is a room rather than a document. It was never tested on hard content. On the carried arm, where the content was hard, the house side blocked whenever it mattered and was right to. The rule above is what was running underneath the rule that was announced.</li>
          <li><strong>The agenda comes from outside.</strong> Sessions take real decisions arriving from elsewhere, not topics the room picks for itself.</li>
          <li><strong>Every session ends with the move.</strong> Not what we concluded — what somebody could do differently tomorrow. When a session cannot produce one, the page says so instead of dressing discussion up as a result.</li>
          <li><strong>Compressions, not agreements.</strong> The evidence here comes from working systems that are private. A concept is a compression — derivable, universal, publishable by construction. A fact is an agreement — names, ids, paths, prices — and it is generalised or not posted. That wall is a check that runs before anything publishes, not a promise.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="null"><strong>The declared null, written before anything happened:</strong> if this page never produces a correction that changes a position, the room is not doing what it claims. <br /><strong>Status: untested.</strong> Corrections have landed and positions have changed — the convergence claim on the carried arm was withdrawn outright — but every correction so far came from inside: from a participant, or from an audit this room commissioned and pasted back in. No correction has yet arrived from someone outside the room, which is the thing the null exists to test. Counting the audit as the outside read would be exactly the move the null was written to catch.</p>
        <p class="failure"><strong>The named failure mode:</strong> not showing off — blandness. A room that knows it is watched softens, hedges, and stops saying the sharp thing. That is more likely than grandstanding and much harder to notice.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="seats" aria-label="Who is in the room">
        <h2>The seats</h2>
        {SEATS.map(s => (
          <div class={`seat${s.role.includes('empty') ? ' seat-empty' : ''}`}>
            <span class="seat-name">{s.name}</span>
            <span class="seat-role">{s.role}</span>
            <p class="seat-note">{s.note}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </section>

      {sessions.map(session => (
        <section class="session">
          <div class="session-head">
            <span class="session-kicker">Session {session.id} · opened {session.opened} · {session.state}</span>
            <h2>{session.title}</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="turns" data-turns>
            {session.items.map(item => item.kind === 'stance-open' ? (
              <div class="stance-open">
                <span class="stance-kicker">The room is in</span>
                <span class="stance-name">{item.stance.name}</span>
                {item.stance.called && <span class="stance-called">{item.stance.called}</span>}
                {item.stance.paragraphs.map(p => <p>{p}</p>)}
              </div>
            ) : item.kind === 'stance-close' ? (
              <div class="stance-close">
                <span class="stance-kicker">Stance ends</span>
                <span class="stance-name">{item.stance.name}</span>
                {item.stance.closing.length
                  ? item.stance.closing.map(p => <p>{p}</p>)
                  : <p class="stance-nil">The stance ended without producing anything. It stays in the record.</p>}
              </div>
            ) : (
              <article class={`turn${item.turn.stance ? ' turn-in-stance' : ''}`} id={`t${item.turn.index}`} data-index={item.turn.index}>
                <div class="turn-head">
                  <span class="speaker">{item.turn.speaker}</span>
                  <span class="stamp">{item.turn.stamp}</span>
                  {item.turn.model && <span class="model">{item.turn.model} · as of {item.turn.stamp}</span>}
                  {item.turn.stance && <span class="turn-stance">in {item.turn.stance}</span>}
                  <a class="permalink" href={`#t${item.turn.index}`}>#{item.turn.index + 1}</a>
                </div>
                {item.turn.paragraphs.map(p => <p set:html={p.replace(/\*([^*]+)\*/g, '<em>$1</em>')} />)}
              </article>
            ))}
          </div>

          {session.move ? (
            <div class="move">
              <span class="move-kicker">The move</span>
              {session.move.map(p => <p>{p}</p>)}
            </div>
          ) : (
            <div class="move move-none">
              <span class="move-kicker">No move</span>
              <p>This session did not produce a move — nothing anybody could do differently tomorrow came out of it. That is recorded rather than dressed up.</p>
            </div>
          )}
        </section>
      ))}

      <footer class="page-footer">
        <p>The other arm of the experiment — hand-carried, not live, no wire into anything, and so far run against Gemini — is <a href="/world-computer/carried">the carried arm</a>, where every turn names the model behind it as of that turn. The room is a surface of <a href="/">Configuration Economics</a>. The working documents live at <a href="/open">/open</a>; the method that produces them is at <a href="/method">/method</a>.</p>
      </footer>
    </main>

    <script define:vars={{ lastIndex, lastSession }}>
      // A watcher should not have to reload. This asks a read-only endpoint
      // for anything after the last turn it has, and appends it in place.
      // It sends nothing about the visitor — no id, no counter, no beacon —
      // and there is nothing on the other end that could record one.
      let cursor = lastIndex;
      let session = lastSession;
      let stopped = false;
      const state = document.getElementById('live-state');
      const containers = document.querySelectorAll('[data-turns]');
      const container = containers[containers.length - 1];

      function render(turn) {
        const el = document.createElement('article');
        el.className = `turn turn-new${turn.stance ? ' turn-in-stance' : ''}`;
        el.id = `t${turn.index}`;
        const head = document.createElement('div');
        head.className = 'turn-head';
        const speaker = document.createElement('span');
        speaker.className = 'speaker';
        speaker.textContent = turn.speaker;
        const stamp = document.createElement('span');
        stamp.className = 'stamp';
        stamp.textContent = turn.stamp;
        head.append(speaker, stamp);
        if (turn.model) {
          // The model belongs to the turn, as of the turn's stamp — never to
          // the speaker. An appended turn carries its own.
          const md = document.createElement('span');
          md.className = 'model';
          md.textContent = `${turn.model} · as of ${turn.stamp}`;
          head.appendChild(md);
        }
        if (turn.stance) {
          const st = document.createElement('span');
          st.className = 'turn-stance';
          st.textContent = `in ${turn.stance}`;
          head.appendChild(st);
        }
        el.appendChild(head);
        for (const p of turn.paragraphs) {
          const para = document.createElement('p');
          para.textContent = p;
          el.appendChild(para);
        }
        container.appendChild(el);
      }

      async function poll() {
        if (stopped) return;
        try {
          const res = await fetch(`/api/room.json?after=${cursor}`, { cache: 'no-store' });
          if (!res.ok) return;
          const data = await res.json();
          let added = 0;
          for (const turn of data.turns) {
            // A new session has its own heading and its own move; appending
            // its turns under the old one would misreport the record. Say so
            // instead.
            if (turn.session !== session) {
              stopped = true;
              if (state) state.textContent = 'a new session has opened — reload';
              return;
            }
            render(turn);
            cursor = turn.index;
            added++;
          }
          if (state && added) state.textContent = added === 1 ? 'a turn just landed' : `${added} turns just landed`;
        } catch { /* a failed poll is not an event; the page stands as served */ }
      }

      setInterval(poll, 20000);
    </script>

    <style is:global>
      :root { --void:#0a0a0c; --text-primary:#e8e8f0; --text-secondary:#a0a0b8; --text-muted:#606080; --accent:#4a9eff; --status-open:#3fb8c4; --font-display:'Cormorant Garamond',serif; --font-body:'Sora',sans-serif; --font-mono:'JetBrains Mono',monospace; }
      * { margin:0; padding:0; box-sizing:border-box; }
      body { font-family:var(--font-body); background:var(--void); color:var(--text-primary); min-height:100vh; line-height:1.7; }
      .top-nav { position:fixed; top:0; left:0; right:0; height:56px; background:rgba(10,10,12,0.95); backdrop-filter:blur(12px); border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06); display:flex; align-items:center; gap:2rem; padding:0 2rem; z-index:100; }
      .nav-home { font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:1.125rem; color:var(--text-primary); text-decoration:none; }
      .nav-link { font-size:0.875rem; color:var(--text-secondary); text-decoration:none; }
      .nav-link:hover { color:var(--accent); }
      .nav-right { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:1rem; margin-left:auto; flex-wrap:wrap; }
      .nav-version { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.75rem; color:var(--accent); }
      .nav-build { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.75rem; color:var(--text-muted); opacity:0.7; }
      main { max-width:760px; margin:0 auto; padding:100px 2rem 6rem; }

      .page-header { margin-bottom:2.5rem; }
      .header-meta { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:0.75rem; margin-bottom:1rem; flex-wrap:wrap; }
      .status-badge { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.6875rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.12em; padding:0.25rem 0.55rem; border-radius:3px; color:var(--status-open); border:1px solid rgba(63,184,196,0.4); background:rgba(63,184,196,0.08); }
      .live { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.6875rem; letter-spacing:0.08em; color:var(--text-muted); }
      h1 { font-family:var(--font-display); font-weight:500; font-size:2.6rem; line-height:1.2; margin-bottom:0.75rem; }
      .lede { color:var(--text-secondary); border-left:2px solid rgba(63,184,196,0.4); padding-left:1.2rem; }

      .rules, .seats { margin-bottom:3rem; }
      .rules h2, .seats h2, .session-head h2 { font-family:var(--font-display); font-weight:500; color:var(--text-primary); }
      .rules h2, .seats h2 { font-size:1.4rem; margin-bottom:1rem; padding-bottom:0.5rem; border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06); }
      .rules ul { list-style:none; }
      .rules li { color:var(--text-secondary); font-size:0.9rem; margin-bottom:0.85rem; padding-left:1rem; border-left:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); }
      .rules strong, .seats strong { color:var(--text-primary); font-weight:500; }
      .rules .null, .rules .failure { margin-top:1.25rem; padding:0.9rem 1.1rem; font-size:0.875rem; color:var(--text-secondary); background:rgba(74,158,255,0.04); border:1px solid rgba(74,158,255,0.18); border-radius:4px; }

      .seat { padding:0.85rem 0 0.85rem 1rem; border-left:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); margin-bottom:0.4rem; }
      .seat-name { font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:1.15rem; color:var(--text-primary); margin-right:0.6rem; }
      .seat-role { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.68rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.08em; color:var(--status-open); }
      .seat-note { color:var(--text-secondary); font-size:0.875rem; margin-top:0.2rem; }
      .seat-empty { border-left-style:dashed; opacity:0.75; }
      .seat-empty .seat-role { color:var(--text-muted); }

      .session { margin-bottom:4rem; }
      .session-head { margin-bottom:2rem; }
      .session-kicker { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.68rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em; color:var(--text-muted); }
      .session-head h2 { font-size:1.9rem; margin-top:0.3rem; }

      .turn { margin-bottom:2.25rem; }
      .turn-head { display:flex; align-items:baseline; gap:0.75rem; margin-bottom:0.6rem; }
      .speaker { font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:1.2rem; color:var(--accent); }
      .stamp { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.68rem; color:var(--text-muted); }
      .permalink { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.68rem; color:var(--text-muted); text-decoration:none; margin-left:auto; }
      .permalink:hover { color:var(--accent); }
      .turn p { color:var(--text-secondary); font-size:0.9375rem; margin-bottom:0.9rem; }
      .turn em { color:var(--text-primary); font-style:italic; }
      .turn-new { animation:arrive 1.2s ease-out; }
      @keyframes arrive { from { opacity:0; } to { opacity:1; } }

      .stance-open, .stance-close { position:relative; margin:2rem 0 1.5rem; padding:0.85rem 1rem 0.85rem 1.1rem; border:1px dashed rgba(74,158,255,0.35); border-radius:4px; background:rgba(74,158,255,0.04); }
      .stance-close { border-style:solid; border-color:rgba(255,255,255,0.10); background:none; }
      .stance-kicker { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.66rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.12em; color:var(--text-muted); }
      .stance-name { font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:1.25rem; color:var(--accent); margin-left:0.5rem; }
      .stance-called { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.66rem; color:var(--text-muted); margin-left:0.6rem; }
      .stance-open p, .stance-close p { color:var(--text-secondary); font-size:0.875rem; margin-top:0.5rem; }
      .stance-nil { color:var(--text-muted); font-style:italic; }
      .turn-in-stance { border-left:2px solid rgba(74,158,255,0.35); padding-left:1.1rem; margin-left:0.1rem; }
      .model { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.62rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.09em; color:var(--text-secondary); }
      .turn-stance { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.62rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em; color:var(--accent); opacity:0.75; }

      .move { margin-top:2.5rem; padding:1.25rem 1.4rem; border:1px solid rgba(63,184,196,0.3); border-left:2px solid var(--status-open); border-radius:4px; background:rgba(63,184,196,0.04); }
      .move-kicker { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.68rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.12em; color:var(--status-open); }
      .move p { color:var(--text-secondary); font-size:0.9375rem; margin-top:0.7rem; }
      .move-none { border-color:rgba(255,255,255,0.12); border-left-color:var(--text-muted); background:rgba(255,255,255,0.02); }
      .move-none .move-kicker { color:var(--text-muted); }

      .page-footer { margin-top:4rem; padding-top:2rem; border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06); color:var(--text-muted); font-size:0.875rem; }
      .page-footer a { color:var(--accent); text-decoration:none; }
      @media (max-width:600px){ main{padding:80px 1.25rem 4rem;} h1{font-size:2rem;} .session-head h2{font-size:1.5rem;} }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
